{{#if length != "FREE"}}{{// Word target for the story text. The header and the ledger don't count.}}{{trim}}
<length>
{{#if length == "SHORT"}}Aim for about 150 to 300 words of story.{{else if length == "LONG"}}Aim for about 600 to 900 words of story.{{else}}Aim for about 350 to 600 words of story.{{/if}} Within that, the scene decides: a quick exchange runs shorter and a big moment runs longer. Earlier reply lengths in the chat don't set the target. Story time moves at the pace of what's happening: a fight moves in seconds, a conversation in exchanges, a trip in hours. Skip quickly over routine in-between moments and linger where attention, emotion, or a decision matters. Spend the words on depth, not distance: the room, bodies, small actions, pauses, and what goes unsaid inside this one beat. The target is never a reason to move the scene forward; when the beat is done, the reply is done, even if it comes in short.
</length>{{/if}}

{{#if extras contains "GRIT"}}{{// Grounded, physical violence for apocalypse and crime stories.}}{{trim}}
<violence>
Violence is sudden, clumsy, and costly. Injuries are specific and physically real: where the blade went in, what broke, how much blood there is. They hurt, they slow people down for days, and they scar. Fights end fast and badly, and the aftermath stays in bodies and in relationships.
</violence>{{/if}}

